==German==

===Etymology===
From {{der|de|gmh|immer}} (also {{m|gmh|iemer}}, {{m|gmh|imer}}), from {{der|de|goh|iomer|iomēr|always}}. From {{compound|io|mer|alt2=mēr||t1=always|t2=more|lang=goh|nocat=1}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|immer}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈɪmɐ/|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-at-immer.ogg|audio (Austria)|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-immer.ogg|Audio|lang=de}}

===Adverb===
{{de-adv}}

# [[always]]
# {{lb|de|with [[Appendix:Glossary#comparative|comparative]]}} [[more and more]]
#: {{uxi|de|Es wird '''immer''' kälter.|It's getting colder and colder.}}
# {{lb|de|colloquial|unstressed}} {{non-gloss definition|used to emphasize another adverb of time, which itself is strongly stressed}}
#: {{ux|de|Er kommt '''immer''' nie pünktlich.|He’s never on time.}}
#: {{ux|de|Ich bin oft '''immer''' sehr vergesslich.|I’m often very forgetful.}}
#: {{ux|de|Manchmal hab ich '''immer''' das Gefühl, dass...|Sometimes I get the feeling that...}}

